      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T17:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`enum class` doesn\u0027t have implicit conversion to ints, so we don\u0027t want it strongly typed. Maybe this is another reason to unflatten the slot infos?",
      "parentUuid": "2f1cfc5a_6198b3b8",
      "revId": "607a1f126e20d8a1f2dec111d378a239a5cb9d84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "399eb69d_bcc62ef1",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/include/SlotManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T14:13:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of storing in fSlotInfos, would it make sense to generate on the fly?  The information is already present in SlotMaps.\n\nI\u0027m assuming this is called rarely (once?), so performance is not an issue.\n\nAlso, currently we\u0027re flattening all types into a single array, but then the client needs to separate again based on the type tag.  It seems it would be less friction to return separate arrays for different types (then I think we don\u0027t need the enum at all).\n\nI\u0027m thinking something along the lines of\n\n    struct SlotInfo {\n        std::vector\u003cSlotID\u003e fScalarSlots;\n        std::vector\u003cSlotID\u003e fColorSlots;\n        ...\n    };\n    \n    SlotInfo getSlotInfo() const {\n        SlotInfo sinfo;\n    \n        sinfo.fScalarSlots.reserve(fScalarMap.count());\n        for (const auto\u0026 scalar : fScalarMap) {\n            sinfo.fScalarSlots.push_back(scalar.first);\n        }\n        \n        ...\n        \n        return sinfo;\n    }\n    \nWDYT?",
      "revId": "607a1f126e20d8a1f2dec111d378a239a5cb9d84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a8aed85_7ce056e1",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/include/SlotManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 11964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T17:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It makes sense, I\u0027m on the fence. Getting rid of the enum is nice and runtime is definitely negligible. I\u0027m worried about if we add more slot types in the future we have to account for clients having to update their code. Thinking about canvas kit, if the SlotInfo struct changes, we have to update CK\u0027s `ManagedAnimation`. It\u0027s easier for other clients to update their code as well.\n\nEither way, we could generate it on the fly.",
      "parentUuid": "399eb69d_bcc62ef1",
      "revId": "607a1f126e20d8a1f2dec111d378a239a5cb9d84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
